From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Solaceon drawn on east past its border (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

East of Solaceon Town the overworld has the mountain's filler map (land
data 175): with the wider view, from the town's east side its tree rows,
plateau and cliffs stopped on a straight line at the border, the
filler's flat top past it. Solaceon joins the maps drawn on straight
past the scenery beside them (sPortMirroredBesideScenery, extruded), on
its east side only: its strip by the border goes on east.
---
diff --git a/src/overlay005/land_data.c b/src/overlay005/land_data.c
index 20b852a6..d9633576 100644
--- a/src/overlay005/land_data.c
+++ b/src/overlay005/land_data.c
@@ -2067,7 +2067,10 @@ static void Port_RenderSceneryMapsLowered(const LandDataManager *landDataMan)
 // the maps' own paths, cliffs and windmills showed again backwards
 // (rejected, 2026-11-07): each listed is now drawn on straight past the
 // scenery (extruded, Port_RenderExtrudedEdge), its forest, cliffs, river
-// and mountain going on.
+// and mountain going on. Solaceon's east side saw the mountain scenery's
+// flat top past its border, its own tree rows and cliffs stopping on a
+// straight line there (a screenshot of 2026-11-07, by a cave entrance):
+// drawn on east, they go on.
 typedef struct PortMirroredScenery {
     u16 header;
     s8 side;     // (the side it's drawn past the scenery on: 0 either, -1 the left only, 1 the right only)
@@ -2080,6 +2083,7 @@ static const PortMirroredScenery sPortMirroredBesideScenery[] = {
     { MAP_HEADER_ROUTE_204_NORTH, 0, TRUE },
     { MAP_HEADER_ROUTE_204_SOUTH, 0, TRUE },
     { MAP_HEADER_HEARTHOME_CITY, -1, TRUE },
+    { MAP_HEADER_SOLACEON_TOWN, 1, TRUE },
 };
 
 static BOOL Port_ExtrudedBesideScenery(u16 header)
